The training set is for model fitting and cross-validation. The validation set is for model comparison, hyperparameter decisions, probability-threshold selection, and other model-selection decisions. The final test set is reserved for one final, unbiased evaluation after the modeling decisions have been completed.

**Do not repeatedly evaluate the test set to choose a model, tune a threshold, or modify the pipeline.**

Use stratification because machine failure is a minority class. Verify that each split contains both target classes.

If the split or validation set is too small for a reliable conclusion, explain the limitation and propose a statistically defensible alternative. Do not silently change the split just to improve scores.

Use stratified cross-validation within the training set for robust comparisons and hyperparameter tuning. Keep every data-dependent transformation inside the cross-validation pipeline.

Never apply SMOTE, oversampling, undersampling, or any other resampling method before splitting the data. If resampling is considered, apply it only inside training folds and compare it against simpler alternatives.

